.TH MRQ 1
.SH NAME
mrq \- a Markdown toolkit for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmrq\fR \fBvalidate\fR [\fIoptions\fR] [\fIpath\fR...]
.br
\fBmrq\fR \fBrender\fR \fB\-o\fR \fIformat\fR [\fIpath\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmrq\fR verifies, lints, formats and \fIrenders\fR Markdown, with \fBcode\fR, \fBboth\fR and
\fB\-\-dashes\fR. Backslashes \\ and dashes \- are escaped, so are the
\&.leading dot and the
\*(Aqleading quote. It\*(Aqs fine.
.br
After a hard break, a line can start
\&.with a dot too.
.PP
See the README <https://github.com/mtrense/marquee> or https://example.com,
a section and another page.
An image: the logo. A footnote[1] and another[2].
.SH OPTIONS
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIformat\fR:
The output format.
.IP \(bu 2
A loose item.
.RS 2
.PP
With a second paragraph.
.IP \(bu 2
Nested
.IP \(bu 2
Items
.RE
.IP 1. 3
First
.IP 2. 3
Second
.RS 3
.IP 1. 3
Inner
.RE
